node_modules
# No trailing slash (bc-slxm): a pattern ending in `/` matches **directories only**, and
# for a while a worktree's `public/vendor` *was* a symlink to the main checkout's copy —
# that is what left it unmatched and showing as `?? public/vendor`, which made
# bin/deliver.js refuse a worktree with uncommitted changes in it, at the very end, after
# the suite had already passed.
#
# `node scripts/vendor.js` (run automatically in a fresh worktree) no longer symlinks the
# directory itself: `public/vendor` is a real directory holding one symlink per bundle to
# the main checkout's copy (bc-oqu7/bc-mf9s) — a real directory holding seven links is
# ignored exactly as one holding seven copies is, so the trailing-slash question no longer
# applies either way. Don't "fix" a worktree by replacing `public/vendor` with one symlink
# to the whole directory: it still passes this pattern, but git then refuses to resolve
# *any* path underneath it ('fatal: pathspec ... is beyond a symbolic link'), which is
# exactly what test/gitignoreresidue.mjs hits (bc-0i27.25). Re-run `node scripts/vendor.js`
# instead if `public/vendor` is ever a bare symlink.
# `node_modules` above has always been spelled this way, which is why only vendor bit.
public/vendor
*.log

# Per-session working notes, not part of the product. They also tend to quote
# machine-local details — the ntfy topic name, absolute paths, unrelated projects —
# which is exactly what you don't want in a repo you hand to someone else.
.claude/handoffs/

# Screenshots from `node scripts/shot.mjs`, written for an agent to Read and then
# forget. Every one of them is a picture of real beads — titles, workspaces, whatever
# was on screen — so they belong to the machine that took them and nowhere else.
.claude/shots/

# Soft-deleted worktrees, kept on disk so a finished session stays resumable, plus a
# .note saying what was retired and when. Local scratch like the two above — and the
# reason to ignore rather than merely leave untracked is that each one is a whole
# checkout, so a stray `git add .` in the main repo commits dozens of them at once.
.claude/worktrees-retired/

# Built and published by `npm run android` — 28 MB, and rebuilt from source.
public/beadcause.apk
# What that build writes beside it: the versionCode, the size and the digest, so the
# daemon can say which build is published without unpacking an APK (lib/update.js).
# Published with the file it describes and committed for the same reason it is not.
public/beadcause.apk.json

# Android build output and machine-local SDK path.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
*.apk
*.keystore
*.jks

# Machine residue in whatever checkout somebody opened, and neither is ours: the Finder
# writes `.DS_Store` into any folder it displays, and a JetBrains IDE writes `.idea/` at
# the root of any project it opens. Untracked residue no longer refuses a delivery's
# fast-forward (bc-45g8) — but the *shared* main checkout is where these two land, every
# session on this Mac reads its `git status`, and two `??` lines that nobody may clear,
# because they come straight back, make a dirty tree the resting state. `android/.idea/`
# above has been ignored since the app existed, which is the tell that the root one was
# an oversight rather than a decision. Anchored with a leading slash so it is the repo
# root's IDE project and not, say, a fixture named `.idea` somewhere under test/.
.DS_Store
/.idea/

# scripts/coverage.mjs — the raw NODE_V8_COVERAGE output, one JSON per process the run
# spawned, tens of megabytes a slice. It is a claim about this checkout only, it is
# regenerated by the next measurement, and the folded report that anything actually
# reads is published to ~/.config/beadcause/coverage.json instead.
.coverage/

# Generated by scripts/design/build.mjs — the Claude Design bundle is derived from
# public/style.css and scripts/design/manifest.mjs, so the generator is the source and
# this is the output. Rebuild it with `node scripts/design/build.mjs`.
design-bundle

# Screenshots from scripts/design/shots.mjs — 154 PNGs, regenerated on demand.
design-shots
